/**
 * Port of Workshop/Workshop.cs (client surface): a catalog of content made by players and the
 * publisher, and LICENSES to it. Nothing is transferred: acquiring grants access to a digital copy,
 * the author keeps it.
 *
 * - Publishing is `publish(...)`: it declares the files, uploads the bytes straight to storage by
 *   signed URLs, then asks the server to verify and release them. The server re-checks sizes and
 *   file signatures itself — the declaration guarantees nothing.
 * - Getting something is `acquire(content, option)`: pass the option from `content.Access` so the
 *   price you showed is the price you pay (`ExpectedPrice` — a changed price is refused, not charged).
 * - Opening it is `downloadFiles(contentID)`: short-lived signed links, fetched right away.
 */
